    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0363" n="257" xml:id="pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00 Congress, Communist International, VII/96:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-30T13:00:00+03:00">August 30, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 30—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>401. The full resolutions of the Congress of the Communist International were
                    published yesterday by <hi rendition="#italic">Pravda</hi>. There is no
                    important reference to the United States. The resolution on Dimitrov’s report contains a full general
                    program for world revolution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
